{
  "requirement": "For node reads, the SDK constructs a `Snapshot` from\nthe contents returned by `Domain::node_content` and their\n`NodeContents::fingerprint` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint`, without another read.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct Snapshot<T> {\n    pub content: T,\n    pub fingerprint: Fingerprint,\n}\n\nimpl<T> Snapshot<T> {\n    pub fn new(content: T, fingerprint: Fingerprint) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<T: Clone> Clone for Snapshot<T>;\nimpl<T: Debug> Debug for Snapshot<T>;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately cover `requirements.sdk.graph.snapshot`.\n\n**Obligations and the tests that cover them**\n- **Public type and constructor.** `Snapshot::new` must pair a content value with a fingerprint, and both fields must be public. `tests/contracts.rs#fn[callers_can_pair_content_with_its_fingerprint]` builds a `Snapshot` with `Snapshot::new` and asserts `content` and `fingerprint`. The test is in an external crate, so it also exercises the public API.\n- **Construction from `Domain::node_content` and `NodeContents::fingerprint`.**\n  - `src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots]` asserts that `read_snapshot` returns content equal to the original. It runs on an empty string and on a large Unicode string. It also asserts that `snapshot.fingerprint == fp(original)`.\n  - `src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` asserts `read_snapshot(&1).fingerprint == fp(\"before\")`. It then changes the node and shows that later reads yield a distinct version.\n  - `tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` asserts `snapshot.content.fingerprint() == snapshot.fingerprint`.\n  - `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` asserts that the retained content's fingerprint equals the fingerprint the domain derives.\n- **\"Without another read\".**\n  - `fn[direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots]` asserts the read log is `[1, 1]` after one `read_snapshot` and one `read`. That is one read per call.\n  - `fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` asserts the read log is `[1]`. It also asserts that the snapshot's fingerprint and content still say \"before\" after the node changed to \"after\". The fingerprint therefore comes from the retained content, not from a re-read.\n  - `fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` asserts a read log of `[1, 1, 1, 2]` across its calls.\n- **Agent-driven reads.** `src/agent/tests.rs#fn[graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery]` checks that the snapshot fingerprint recorded as a `Dependency::Node` matches the full content delivered through the agent's `read_node` tool. The agent-facing tests in `fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` and `fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]` also carry `{test}` references to this requirement. They exercise the same snapshot flow through the agent. The second one covers edge reads.\n\n**Not directly tested: `Clone` and `Debug`**\n- `Snapshot` gets `Clone` and `Debug` from `#[derive(Clone, Debug)]` in `src/graph.rs#struct[Snapshot]`. The derives have no conditionals and no transformation of their own.\n- `#[non_exhaustive]` is a compile-time attribute with no runtime behavior. The external-crate test uses `Snapshot::new` rather than a struct literal, which is consistent with it.\n- I treat these as exempt from needing a test of their own.\n\nI found no gap, and the acknowledgments list is empty.",
  "references": "6783b2a4d0b4e2c98352e3255d1bb07342bc13f8749e2cee76ad5948eb461b69",
